;; CROSS-SOURCE ALIGNMENT of one page's words: correspondence groups (P7.1; SPEC 9.2; D202, D252-D254). emon's own module (D039).
;; It is `emon.xalign` and not `emon.align` because `emon.align` is the paragraph alignment of P4.11 (`al-line`, `al-pass`; D252).
;;
;;   (xa-page page epages words owords tlines feats etext refs cg scr gp dp ta tb tt)
;;       Aligns the text layer (`words`: the visible ones, and the `hidden-text` ones), every OCR run's words (`owords`) and the
;;       tracer's text lines (`tlines`) of ONE page into correspondence groups: rows appended to `cg` (SPEC 9.7), their candidate
;;       runs appended to `refs` as `(ea, index)` pairs, and the similarity columns written into the words' `feats` rows
;;       (`xt-sim-ocr`, `xt-sim-ocr2`, `xo-sim-text`, `xo-sim-hidden`, columns 24 and 25). Answers the number of groups appended.
;;       `scr gp dp ta tb tt` are scratch the caller owns (any contents; they are emptied here): the caller keeps them between pages
;;       so a page costs no allocation once they have grown.
;;
;; WHAT IT READS. The HEADS (SPEC 8.4.1) and nothing else of a word: its page, box, angle, direction, text run, line and feature row
;; (the three kinds of row share the head, D096). A text-layer word is a CANDIDATE of the visible text layer when its `src` is
;; `text` and its worst glyph `vis` (feature column `xt-vis`) is 0 (no feature row, or -1: 0), a candidate of the HIDDEN layer when
;; its `src` is `hidden-text`, and is not a candidate at all otherwise (it is the ledger's). Every OCR word of the page is a candidate,
;; of whichever run made it. The rows of one page are contiguous and pages ascend in each arena (a law holds the builders to it).
;;
;; THE ALGORITHM, as SPEC 9.2 says, with the choices it leaves (D253):
;;   1. A 64 x 64 GRID over the page box indexes every candidate's head. An OCR word is a candidate of a text-layer word when
;;      `ev-overlap-small` of their boxes is at least `xa-overlap` (500) and their angles differ by at most `xa-angle` (300
;;      centi-degrees). The text-layer line of the candidate with the most overlap (ties: the earlier word) is the OCR word's LINE;
;;      an OCR word with no candidate has none.
;;   2. Per text-layer line (a maximal run of consecutive candidates with the same `line`), per layer (visible, then hidden), per OCR
;;      run: the line's OCR words, ordered by their position along the line's baseline (reversed for a right-to-left line, so both
;;      sides are in logical order), are aligned to its words by a DYNAMIC PROGRAM over the two sequences. A step is 1:1, 1:2, 2:1
;;      (two consecutive words of one side against one of the other), 1:0 or 0:1. A pairing step is allowed only when the merged
;;      boxes are candidates by the test above, and costs 1000 minus the intersection over union of the merged words' EXTENTS ALONG
;;      THE LINE (per mille; not of the boxes, because the sources draw a word's height differently and agree on where it is along
;;      the line); an unmatched word costs `xa-gap` (400). Ties are broken toward 1:1, then 1:2, then 2:1, then an unmatched text-layer word,
;;      then an unmatched OCR word. A line whose table would pass `xa-dpmax` cells is paired greedily along the line instead.
;;   3. A GROUP is a connected set of the chosen steps (union-find; a word of the text layer shared by two runs' steps joins them).
;;      What no step matched is attached when the other source COVERS it: an OCR word that is a candidate of a text-layer word joins
;;      that word's group (flag split), a text-layer word that is a candidate of an OCR word joins its group (flag merged): a word
;;      read as three, a line whose spaces the font does not map (D253). An OCR word still unmatched is OCR-ONLY: it joins a group
;;      only through an OCR word of ANOTHER run that overlaps it by the test above (two engines' reading of the same ink); a
;;      text-layer word still unmatched is TEXT-ONLY. Groups come in the order
;;      of their first candidate: text-layer words in the layer's order, then the OCR-only ones in the engine's.
;;   4. Text similarity is `1000 * (max - lev) / max` over the NFC code points (ligatures expanded) of the two sides' words
;;      concatenated, with case kept (`sim`) and over the letters and digits only, case-folded (`simfold`, the broken-encoding test of
;;      SPEC 9.4). A side is capped at `xa-tcap` code points. The group's two sides are its text-layer words (its hidden ones when it
;;      has none of the visible layer) and the words of the lowest-numbered OCR run in it; -1 where a side is empty. The word columns
;;      are written per step with case kept: a text-layer word's `xt-sim-ocr` from the first run, `xt-sim-ocr2` from the second; an
;;      OCR word's `xo-sim-text` against the visible layer, `xo-sim-hidden` against the hidden one; untouched where no step matched it.
;;   5. A group's `tlines` cell is the tracer line of the page that the group's box overlaps most (the same test; ties: the first).
;;
;; WHAT IT DOES NOT DO: weigh the sources (that is arbitration, P7.3), flag `in-figure` or `in-seal` (P7.7, P7.G), or read pixels.
(ns emon.xalign
  (:require [emon.lang :refer [I32 I64 Cells i64 i32 mul64 add64]]
            [emon.port :refer [cells-len cells-at cells-set cells-push cells-drop]]
            [emon.normalize :refer [nz-nfc nz-flag-ligatures nz-flag-soft-hyphens nz-flag-radicals]]
            [emon.evidence :refer [ev-overlap-small ev-page-row ev-sin ev-cos fe-set fe-get ep-get rf-add rf-count
                                   epf-width epf-height
                                   hd-x0 hd-y0 hd-x1 hd-y1 hd-rot hd-dir hd-tstart hd-tlen hd-line hd-feat
                                   owf-run wf-src ea-words ea-owords
                                   xt-vis xt-sim-ocr xt-sim-ocr2 xo-sim-text xo-sim-hidden]]
            [emon.model :refer [sr-hidden-text]]
            [emon.player :refer [cg-new cg-set cgf-tfirst cgf-tcount cgf-ofirst cgf-ocount cgf-hfirst cgf-hcount cgf-tline
                                 cgf-sim cgf-simfold cgf-flags plg-text-only plg-ocr-only]]
            [kin.lang :refer [defn return let set while if do comment
                              + - * < > <= >= == != and or quot rem bit-and bit-or]]))

;; ------------------------------------------------------------- the settings (SPEC 9.4: named, first values, P10.1 calibrates)

(defn ^:pub ^I32 xa-overlap [] (comment "`align-overlap`: the overlap (per mille of the smaller box) that makes two words candidates.") (return 500))
(defn ^:pub ^I32 xa-angle [] (comment "`align-angle`: the most two candidates' angles may differ (centi-degrees).") (return 300))
(defn ^:pub ^I32 xa-gap [] (comment "`align-gap`: what an unmatched word costs in the dynamic program (a pairing costs 1000 minus its overlap).") (return 400))
(defn ^:pub ^I32 xa-tcap [] (comment "The code points of a side that similarity reads (the first ones).") (return 256))
(defn ^:pub ^I32 xa-dpmax [] (comment "The most cells of one line's dynamic program; a larger line is paired greedily.") (return 1000000))

(defn ^I32 xa-inf [] (return 1000000))

;; ------------------------------------------------------------- the scratch
;; `scr`: the heads table `hb` (stride 12: x0 y0 x1 y1 rot dir tstart tlen feat kind line run) of the N candidates (the page's `words`
;; rows first, then its `owords` rows; `kind` 1 visible text, 2 hidden text, 0 not a candidate, 3 OCR), then 16 arrays of S = N + 1
;; cells indexed by node, then the grid's 4096 heads.
;;   array 0 uf  1 nflag  2 oline  3 orank  4 matched  5 okey  6 ord  7 tmp  8 cnt  9 mem  10 root  11 tlist  12 olist  13 olist2
;;         14 elo  15 ehi (a node's extent along its line, which is what a pairing's cost reads)

(defn ^I32 xa-hb [^Cells scr ^I32 i ^I32 f] (return (cells-at scr (+ (* i 12) f))))

(defn ^I32 xa-hbs [^:mut ^Cells scr ^I32 i ^I32 f ^I32 v]
  (cells-set scr (+ (* i 12) f) v)
  (return 0))

(defn ^I32 xa-a [^Cells scr ^I32 nn ^I32 k ^I32 i] (return (cells-at scr (+ (+ (* 12 nn) (* k nn)) i))))

(defn ^I32 xa-as [^:mut ^Cells scr ^I32 nn ^I32 k ^I32 i ^I32 v]
  (cells-set scr (+ (+ (* 12 nn) (* k nn)) i) v)
  (return 0))

(defn ^I32 xa-grid-base [^I32 nn] (return (* 28 nn)))

;; ------------------------------------------------------------- union-find

(defn ^I32 xa-find [^:mut ^Cells scr ^I32 nn ^I32 i]
  (let [^:mut ^I32 r i
        ^:mut ^I32 p 0
        ^:mut ^I32 q i]
    (set p (xa-a scr nn 0 r))
    (while (!= p r)
      (do (set r p)
          (set p (xa-a scr nn 0 r))))
    (while (!= q r)
      (do (set p (xa-a scr nn 0 q))
          (xa-as scr nn 0 q r)
          (set q p)))
    (return r)))

(defn ^I32 xa-union [^:mut ^Cells scr ^I32 nn ^I32 a ^I32 b]
  (comment "Join the sets of a and b; the root of a set is its smallest node, so a group's first candidate is its root.")
  (let [^I32 ra (xa-find scr nn a)
        ^I32 rb (xa-find scr nn b)]
    (if (< ra rb) (xa-as scr nn 0 rb ra))
    (if (< rb ra) (xa-as scr nn 0 ra rb))
    (return 0)))

;; ------------------------------------------------------------- geometry

(defn ^I32 xa-ang-diff [^I32 a ^I32 b]
  (let [^:mut ^I32 d (- a b)]
    (if (< d 0) (set d (- 0 d)))
    (if (> d 18000) (set d (- 36000 d)))
    (return d)))

(defn ^I32 xa-iou1 [^I32 alo ^I32 ahi ^I32 blo ^I32 bhi]
  (comment "Intersection over union of two intervals along a line, per mille; 0 when they miss or the union is empty.")
  (let [^:mut ^I32 lo alo
        ^:mut ^I32 hi ahi
        ^:mut ^I32 ulo alo
        ^:mut ^I32 uhi ahi]
    (if (> blo lo) (set lo blo))
    (if (< bhi hi) (set hi bhi))
    (if (< blo ulo) (set ulo blo))
    (if (> bhi uhi) (set uhi bhi))
    (if (>= lo hi) (return 0))
    (if (<= uhi ulo) (return 0))
    (return (i32 (quot (mul64 (i64 (- hi lo)) (i64 1000)) (i64 (- uhi ulo)))))))

(defn ^I32 xa-cand [^I32 ax0 ^I32 ay0 ^I32 ax1 ^I32 ay1 ^I32 arot ^I32 bx0 ^I32 by0 ^I32 bx1 ^I32 by1 ^I32 brot]
  (comment "1 when two boxes at two angles are candidates of each other (SPEC 9.2), else 0.")
  (if (> (xa-ang-diff arot brot) (xa-angle)) (return 0))
  (if (< (ev-overlap-small ax0 ay0 ax1 ay1 bx0 by0 bx1 by1) (xa-overlap)) (return 0))
  (return 1))

(defn ^I32 xa-node-cand [^Cells scr ^I32 a ^I32 b]
  (return (xa-cand (xa-hb scr a 0) (xa-hb scr a 1) (xa-hb scr a 2) (xa-hb scr a 3) (xa-hb scr a 4)
                   (xa-hb scr b 0) (xa-hb scr b 1) (xa-hb scr b 2) (xa-hb scr b 3) (xa-hb scr b 4))))

(defn ^I32 xa-ubox [^Cells scr ^I32 nn ^I32 k ^I32 s ^I32 c ^I32 f]
  (comment "One coordinate of the union of the boxes of the c nodes of array k from s: f 0 least x0, 1 least y0, 2 greatest x1, 3 greatest y1.")
  (let [^:mut ^I32 t 0
        ^:mut ^I32 v 0
        ^:mut ^I32 node 0
        ^:mut ^I32 w 0]
    (while (< t c)
      (do (set node (xa-a scr nn k (+ s t)))
          (set w (xa-hb scr node f))
          (if (== t 0)
            (set v w)
            (do (if (and (< f 2) (< w v)) (set v w))
                (if (and (>= f 2) (> w v)) (set v w))))
          (set t (+ t 1))))
    (return v)))

(defn ^I32 xa-hull [^Cells scr ^I32 nn ^I32 k ^I32 s ^I32 c ^I32 which]
  (comment "The hull along the line of the c nodes of array k from s: which 0 its start, 1 its end.")
  (let [^:mut ^I32 t 0
        ^:mut ^I32 v 0
        ^:mut ^I32 w 0
        ^:mut ^I32 node 0]
    (while (< t c)
      (do (set node (xa-a scr nn k (+ s t)))
          (if (== which 0)
            (set w (xa-a scr nn 14 node))
            (set w (xa-a scr nn 15 node)))
          (if (== t 0)
            (set v w)
            (do (if (and (== which 0) (< w v)) (set v w))
                (if (and (== which 1) (> w v)) (set v w))))
          (set t (+ t 1))))
    (return v)))

(defn ^I32 xa-cost [^Cells scr ^I32 nn ^I32 ka ^I32 sa ^I32 ca ^I32 kb ^I32 sb ^I32 cb]
  (comment "The cost of pairing ca nodes of array ka from sa with cb nodes of array kb from sb: `xa-inf` when their merged boxes are")
  (comment "not candidates, else 1000 minus the intersection over union of their extents along the line (per mille). Along the line")
  (comment "and not over the boxes, because the sources draw a word's height differently (a font's ascent and descent, an engine's")
  (comment "ink) and agree on where along the line it is (D253).")
  (let [^I32 ax0 (xa-ubox scr nn ka sa ca 0)
        ^I32 ay0 (xa-ubox scr nn ka sa ca 1)
        ^I32 ax1 (xa-ubox scr nn ka sa ca 2)
        ^I32 ay1 (xa-ubox scr nn ka sa ca 3)
        ^I32 bx0 (xa-ubox scr nn kb sb cb 0)
        ^I32 by0 (xa-ubox scr nn kb sb cb 1)
        ^I32 bx1 (xa-ubox scr nn kb sb cb 2)
        ^I32 by1 (xa-ubox scr nn kb sb cb 3)
        ^I32 na (xa-a scr nn ka sa)
        ^I32 nb (xa-a scr nn kb sb)
        ^I32 ra (xa-hb scr na 4)
        ^I32 rb (xa-hb scr nb 4)]
    (if (== (xa-cand ax0 ay0 ax1 ay1 ra bx0 by0 bx1 by1 rb) 0) (return (xa-inf)))
    (let [^I32 alo (xa-hull scr nn ka sa ca 0)
          ^I32 ahi (xa-hull scr nn ka sa ca 1)
          ^I32 blo (xa-hull scr nn kb sb cb 0)
          ^I32 bhi (xa-hull scr nn kb sb cb 1)]
      (return (- 1000 (xa-iou1 alo ahi blo bhi))))))

;; ------------------------------------------------------------- text similarity

(defn ^I32 xa-fold-cp [^I32 cp]
  (comment "A code point's folded form when it is a letter or a digit, 0 when it is not (a space, a punctuation, a symbol).")
  (comment "Case folding covers ASCII, Latin-1, Latin Extended-A, Greek and Cyrillic; every other letter folds to itself.")
  (if (< cp 48) (return 0))
  (if (<= cp 57) (return cp))
  (if (< cp 65) (return 0))
  (if (<= cp 90) (return (+ cp 32)))
  (if (< cp 97) (return 0))
  (if (<= cp 122) (return cp))
  (if (< cp 170) (return 0))
  (if (== cp 170) (return cp))
  (if (< cp 181) (return 0))
  (if (== cp 181) (return cp))
  (if (< cp 186) (return 0))
  (if (== cp 186) (return cp))
  (if (< cp 192) (return 0))
  (if (== cp 215) (return 0))
  (if (== cp 247) (return 0))
  (if (<= cp 222) (return (+ cp 32)))
  (if (<= cp 255) (return cp))
  (if (and (>= cp 256) (<= cp 311))
    (do (if (== (rem cp 2) 0) (return (+ cp 1)))
        (return cp)))
  (if (and (>= cp 313) (<= cp 328))
    (do (if (== (rem cp 2) 1) (return (+ cp 1)))
        (return cp)))
  (if (and (>= cp 330) (<= cp 375))
    (do (if (== (rem cp 2) 0) (return (+ cp 1)))
        (return cp)))
  (if (== cp 376) (return 255))
  (if (and (>= cp 377) (<= cp 382))
    (do (if (== (rem cp 2) 1) (return (+ cp 1)))
        (return cp)))
  (if (and (>= cp 913) (<= cp 937) (!= cp 930)) (return (+ cp 32)))
  (if (and (>= cp 1024) (<= cp 1039)) (return (+ cp 80)))
  (if (and (>= cp 1040) (<= cp 1071)) (return (+ cp 32)))
  (if (and (>= cp 8192) (<= cp 8303)) (return 0))
  (if (and (>= cp 8592) (<= cp 11263)) (return 0))
  (if (and (>= cp 12288) (<= cp 12351)) (return 0))
  (if (and (>= cp 65024) (<= cp 65039)) (return 0))
  (if (== cp 65279) (return 0))
  (return cp))

(defn ^I32 xa-fold-in-place [^:mut ^Cells c]
  (comment "Keep the letters and digits of c, case-folded, in order.")
  (let [^I32 n (cells-len c)
        ^:mut ^I32 i 0
        ^:mut ^I32 j 0
        ^:mut ^I32 f 0
        ^:mut ^I32 cp 0]
    (while (< i n)
      (do (set cp (cells-at c i))
          (set f (xa-fold-cp cp))
          (if (!= f 0)
            (do (cells-set c j f)
                (set j (+ j 1))))
          (set i (+ i 1))))
    (cells-drop c j)
    (return j)))

(defn ^I32 xa-side [^Cells scr ^I32 nn ^I32 k ^I32 s ^I32 c ^Cells etext ^:mut ^Cells out ^:mut ^Cells tt]
  (comment "Empty `out` and fill it with the NFC code points (ligatures expanded) of the c nodes of array k from s, side by side, the first `xa-tcap`.")
  (let [^:mut ^I32 t 0
        ^:mut ^I32 node 0
        ^:mut ^I32 ts 0
        ^:mut ^I32 tl 0]
    (cells-drop out 0)
    (while (< t c)
      (do (set node (xa-a scr nn k (+ s t)))
          (set ts (xa-hb scr node 6))
          (set tl (xa-hb scr node 7))
          (if (> tl 0)
            (nz-nfc etext ts (+ ts tl) out tt (+ (nz-flag-ligatures) (+ (nz-flag-soft-hyphens) (nz-flag-radicals)))))
          (set t (+ t 1))))
    (if (> (cells-len out) (xa-tcap)) (cells-drop out (xa-tcap)))
    (return (cells-len out))))

(defn ^I32 xa-lev [^Cells a ^Cells b ^:mut ^Cells tt]
  (comment "The Levenshtein distance of a and b (code points), its two rows in `tt`.")
  (let [^I32 la (cells-len a)
        ^I32 lb (cells-len b)
        ^:mut ^I32 j 0
        ^:mut ^I32 i 1
        ^:mut ^I32 sub 0
        ^:mut ^I32 best 0
        ^:mut ^I32 alt 0
        ^:mut ^I32 up 0
        ^:mut ^I32 left 0
        ^:mut ^I32 diag 0
        ^:mut ^I32 ca 0
        ^:mut ^I32 cb 0
        ^:mut ^I32 prev 0]
    (cells-drop tt 0)
    (while (< j (* 2 (+ lb 1)))
      (do (cells-push tt 0)
          (set j (+ j 1))))
    (set j 0)
    (while (<= j lb)
      (do (cells-set tt j j)
          (set j (+ j 1))))
    (while (<= i la)
      (do (cells-set tt (+ lb 1) i)
          (set ca (cells-at a (- i 1)))
          (set j 1)
          (while (<= j lb)
            (do (set diag (cells-at tt (- j 1)))
                (set up (cells-at tt j))
                (set left (cells-at tt (+ (+ lb 1) (- j 1))))
                (set cb (cells-at b (- j 1)))
                (set sub 1)
                (if (== ca cb) (set sub 0))
                (set best (+ diag sub))
                (set alt (+ up 1))
                (if (< alt best) (set best alt))
                (set alt (+ left 1))
                (if (< alt best) (set best alt))
                (cells-set tt (+ (+ lb 1) j) best)
                (set j (+ j 1))))
          (set j 0)
          (while (<= j lb)
            (do (set prev (cells-at tt (+ (+ lb 1) j)))
                (cells-set tt j prev)
                (set j (+ j 1))))
          (set i (+ i 1))))
    (return (cells-at tt lb))))

(defn ^I32 xa-sim [^Cells scr ^I32 nn ^I32 ka ^I32 sa ^I32 ca ^I32 kb ^I32 sb ^I32 cb ^Cells etext ^I32 fold
                   ^:mut ^Cells ta ^:mut ^Cells tb ^:mut ^Cells tt]
  (comment "The similarity (per mille) of two sides, each some consecutive nodes of an array: case kept (fold 0) or over the")
  (comment "case-folded letters and digits only (fold 1). Both sides empty is 1000.")
  (xa-side scr nn ka sa ca etext ta tt)
  (xa-side scr nn kb sb cb etext tb tt)
  (if (== fold 1)
    (do (xa-fold-in-place ta)
        (xa-fold-in-place tb)))
  (let [^I32 la (cells-len ta)
        ^I32 lb (cells-len tb)
        ^:mut ^I32 mx la]
    (if (> lb mx) (set mx lb))
    (if (== mx 0) (return 1000))
    (let [^I32 d (xa-lev ta tb tt)]
      (return (quot (* (- mx d) 1000) mx)))))

;; ------------------------------------------------------------- columns

(defn ^I32 xa-put [^Cells scr ^I32 node ^I32 col ^I32 v ^:mut ^Cells feats]
  (comment "Write `v` into column `col` of the node's feature row, when it has one.")
  (let [^I32 row (xa-hb scr node 8)]
    (if (>= row 0) (fe-set feats row col v))
    (return 0)))

;; ------------------------------------------------------------- the steps

(defn ^I32 xa-step [^:mut ^Cells scr ^I32 nn ^I32 ts ^I32 tc ^I32 os ^I32 oc ^I32 layer ^I32 rank
                    ^Cells etext ^:mut ^Cells feats ^:mut ^Cells ta ^:mut ^Cells tb ^:mut ^Cells tt]
  (comment "One chosen pairing step: the text-layer nodes `tlist[ts, ts + tc)` with the OCR nodes `olist2[os, os + oc)`. Join them,")
  (comment "mark a 1:2 as a split and a 2:1 as merged, record that the OCR nodes were matched, and write the similarity columns")
  (comment "(`layer` 1 the visible layer, 2 the hidden one).")
  (let [^I32 sim (xa-sim scr nn 11 ts tc 13 os oc etext 0 ta tb tt)
        ^I32 head (xa-a scr nn 11 ts)
        ^:mut ^I32 t 0
        ^:mut ^I32 node 0
        ^:mut ^I32 fl 0
        ^:mut ^I32 cur 0]
    (if (and (== tc 1) (== oc 2)) (set fl 4))
    (if (and (== tc 2) (== oc 1)) (set fl 8))
    (while (< t tc)
      (do (set node (xa-a scr nn 11 (+ ts t)))
          (xa-union scr nn head node)
          (xa-as scr nn 4 node 1)
          (set cur (xa-a scr nn 1 node))
          (xa-as scr nn 1 node (bit-or cur fl))
          (if (== rank 0) (xa-put scr node (xt-sim-ocr) sim feats))
          (if (== rank 1) (xa-put scr node (xt-sim-ocr2) sim feats))
          (set t (+ t 1))))
    (set t 0)
    (while (< t oc)
      (do (set node (xa-a scr nn 13 (+ os t)))
          (xa-union scr nn head node)
          (xa-as scr nn 4 node 1)
          (set cur (xa-a scr nn 1 node))
          (xa-as scr nn 1 node (bit-or cur fl))
          (if (== layer 1) (xa-put scr node (xo-sim-text) sim feats))
          (if (== layer 2) (xa-put scr node (xo-sim-hidden) sim feats))
          (set t (+ t 1))))
    (return 0)))

(defn ^I32 xa-greedy [^:mut ^Cells scr ^I32 nn ^I32 n ^I32 m ^I32 layer ^I32 rank ^Cells etext ^:mut ^Cells feats
                      ^:mut ^Cells ta ^:mut ^Cells tb ^:mut ^Cells tt]
  (comment "A line too long for the table: walk the two sequences along the line, pairing 1:1 where the words are candidates and")
  (comment "otherwise leaving the one that lies earlier unmatched.")
  (let [^:mut ^I32 i 0
        ^:mut ^I32 j 0
        ^:mut ^I32 ti 0
        ^:mut ^I32 oj 0
        ^:mut ^I32 kt 0
        ^:mut ^I32 ko 0]
    (while (and (< i n) (< j m))
      (do (if (< (xa-cost scr nn 11 i 1 13 j 1) (xa-inf))
            (do (xa-step scr nn i 1 j 1 layer rank etext feats ta tb tt)
                (set i (+ i 1))
                (set j (+ j 1)))
            (do (set ti (xa-a scr nn 11 i))
                (set oj (xa-a scr nn 13 j))
                (set kt (xa-a scr nn 5 ti))
                (set ko (xa-a scr nn 5 oj))
                (if (<= kt ko)
                  (set i (+ i 1))
                  (set j (+ j 1)))))))
    (return 0)))

(defn ^I32 xa-dp-at [^Cells dp ^I32 m ^I32 i ^I32 j] (return (cells-at dp (+ (* i (+ m 1)) j))))

(defn ^I32 xa-align [^:mut ^Cells scr ^I32 nn ^I32 n ^I32 m ^I32 layer ^I32 rank ^Cells etext ^:mut ^Cells feats
                     ^:mut ^Cells dp ^:mut ^Cells ta ^:mut ^Cells tb ^:mut ^Cells tt]
  (comment "Align the n text-layer nodes of `tlist` with the m OCR nodes of `olist2` (both in logical order along the line) and")
  (comment "apply the steps. The table is `(n + 1) * (m + 1)` costs and then as many choices (1 pair, 2 a 1:2, 3 a 2:1, 4 a text-layer")
  (comment "word alone, 5 an OCR word alone).")
  (if (> (* (+ n 1) (+ m 1)) (xa-dpmax))
    (do (xa-greedy scr nn n m layer rank etext feats ta tb tt)
        (return 0)))
  (let [^I32 sz (* (+ n 1) (+ m 1))
        ^:mut ^I32 k 0
        ^:mut ^I32 i 0
        ^:mut ^I32 j 0
        ^:mut ^I32 best 0
        ^:mut ^I32 choice 0
        ^:mut ^I32 c 0
        ^:mut ^I32 w 0]
    (cells-drop dp 0)
    (while (< k (* 2 sz))
      (do (cells-push dp 0)
          (set k (+ k 1))))
    (while (<= i n)
      (do (set j 0)
          (while (<= j m)
            (do (set best 2000000000)
                (set choice 0)
                (if (and (> i 0) (> j 0))
                  (do (set w (xa-cost scr nn 11 (- i 1) 1 13 (- j 1) 1))
                      (if (< w (xa-inf))
                        (do (set c (+ (xa-dp-at dp m (- i 1) (- j 1)) w))
                            (if (< c best) (do (set best c) (set choice 1)))))))
                (if (and (> i 0) (> j 1))
                  (do (set w (xa-cost scr nn 11 (- i 1) 1 13 (- j 2) 2))
                      (if (< w (xa-inf))
                        (do (set c (+ (xa-dp-at dp m (- i 1) (- j 2)) w))
                            (if (< c best) (do (set best c) (set choice 2)))))))
                (if (and (> i 1) (> j 0))
                  (do (set w (xa-cost scr nn 11 (- i 2) 2 13 (- j 1) 1))
                      (if (< w (xa-inf))
                        (do (set c (+ (xa-dp-at dp m (- i 2) (- j 1)) w))
                            (if (< c best) (do (set best c) (set choice 3)))))))
                (if (> i 0)
                  (do (set c (+ (xa-dp-at dp m (- i 1) j) (xa-gap)))
                      (if (< c best) (do (set best c) (set choice 4)))))
                (if (> j 0)
                  (do (set c (+ (xa-dp-at dp m i (- j 1)) (xa-gap)))
                      (if (< c best) (do (set best c) (set choice 5)))))
                (if (== choice 0) (set best 0))
                (cells-set dp (+ (* i (+ m 1)) j) best)
                (cells-set dp (+ sz (+ (* i (+ m 1)) j)) choice)
                (set j (+ j 1))))
          (set i (+ i 1))))
    (set i n)
    (set j m)
    (while (or (> i 0) (> j 0))
      (do (set choice (cells-at dp (+ sz (+ (* i (+ m 1)) j))))
          (if (== choice 1)
            (do (xa-step scr nn (- i 1) 1 (- j 1) 1 layer rank etext feats ta tb tt)
                (set i (- i 1))
                (set j (- j 1))))
          (if (== choice 2)
            (do (xa-step scr nn (- i 1) 1 (- j 2) 2 layer rank etext feats ta tb tt)
                (set i (- i 1))
                (set j (- j 2))))
          (if (== choice 3)
            (do (xa-step scr nn (- i 2) 2 (- j 1) 1 layer rank etext feats ta tb tt)
                (set i (- i 2))
                (set j (- j 1))))
          (if (== choice 4) (set i (- i 1)))
          (if (== choice 5) (set j (- j 1)))
          (if (== choice 0)
            (do (set i 0)
                (set j 0)))))
    (return 0)))

;; ------------------------------------------------------------- sorting (stable, by a key array)

(defn ^I32 xa-msort [^:mut ^Cells scr ^I32 nn ^I32 arr ^I32 lo ^I32 cnt ^I32 kk]
  (comment "Sort the c nodes of array `arr` from `lo` by the key array `kk` ascending, stably (a bottom-up merge sort through array 7).")
  (let [^:mut ^I32 width 1
        ^:mut ^I32 start 0
        ^:mut ^I32 mid 0
        ^:mut ^I32 hi 0
        ^:mut ^I32 p 0
        ^:mut ^I32 q 0
        ^:mut ^I32 o 0
        ^:mut ^I32 x 0
        ^:mut ^I32 y 0
        ^:mut ^I32 kx 0
        ^:mut ^I32 ky 0]
    (while (< width cnt)
      (do (set start 0)
          (while (< start cnt)
            (do (set mid (+ start width))
                (if (> mid cnt) (set mid cnt))
                (set hi (+ start (* 2 width)))
                (if (> hi cnt) (set hi cnt))
                (set p start)
                (set q mid)
                (set o start)
                (while (or (< p mid) (< q hi))
                  (do (if (>= p mid)
                        (do (set y (xa-a scr nn arr (+ lo q)))
                            (xa-as scr nn 7 o y)
                            (set q (+ q 1)))
                        (if (>= q hi)
                          (do (set x (xa-a scr nn arr (+ lo p)))
                              (xa-as scr nn 7 o x)
                              (set p (+ p 1)))
                          (do (set x (xa-a scr nn arr (+ lo p)))
                              (set y (xa-a scr nn arr (+ lo q)))
                              (set kx (xa-a scr nn kk x))
                              (set ky (xa-a scr nn kk y))
                              (if (<= kx ky)
                                (do (xa-as scr nn 7 o x)
                                    (set p (+ p 1)))
                                (do (xa-as scr nn 7 o y)
                                    (set q (+ q 1)))))))
                      (set o (+ o 1))))
                (set start (+ start (* 2 width)))))
          (set p 0)
          (while (< p cnt)
            (do (set x (xa-a scr nn 7 p))
                (xa-as scr nn arr (+ lo p) x)
                (set p (+ p 1))))
          (set width (* width 2))))
    (return 0)))

;; ------------------------------------------------------------- the grid

(defn ^I32 xa-cell [^I32 x ^I32 size]
  (comment "The grid cell (0..63) of a coordinate on a page `size` wide.")
  (let [^:mut ^I32 v (i32 (quot (mul64 (i64 x) (i64 64)) (i64 size)))]
    (if (< v 0) (set v 0))
    (if (> v 63) (set v 63))
    (return v)))

(defn ^I32 xa-grid-add [^:mut ^Cells scr ^I32 nn ^:mut ^Cells gp ^I32 node ^I32 pw ^I32 ph]
  (comment "Enter a node in every grid cell its box touches.")
  (let [^I32 cx0 (xa-cell (xa-hb scr node 0) pw)
        ^I32 cx1 (xa-cell (xa-hb scr node 2) pw)
        ^I32 cy0 (xa-cell (xa-hb scr node 1) ph)
        ^I32 cy1 (xa-cell (xa-hb scr node 3) ph)
        ^I32 gb (xa-grid-base nn)
        ^:mut ^I32 cy cy0
        ^:mut ^I32 cx 0
        ^:mut ^I32 at 0
        ^:mut ^I32 head 0
        ^:mut ^I32 at2 0]
    (while (<= cy cy1)
      (do (set cx cx0)
          (while (<= cx cx1)
            (do (set at (+ gb (+ (* cy 64) cx)))
                (set head (cells-at scr at))
                (cells-push gp node)
                (cells-push gp head)
                (set at2 (- (cells-len gp) 2))
                (cells-set scr at at2)
                (set cx (+ cx 1))))
          (set cy (+ cy 1))))
    (return 0)))

(defn ^I32 xa-best [^Cells scr ^I32 nn ^Cells gp ^I32 nt ^I32 node ^I32 pw ^I32 ph ^I32 side]
  (comment "The candidate of `node` with the most overlap (`ev-overlap-small`), -1 for none; ties go to the earlier node. `side` 1 looks")
  (comment "among the text layer's candidates, 0 among the OCR words (other than the node itself).")
  (let [^I32 cx0 (xa-cell (xa-hb scr node 0) pw)
        ^I32 cx1 (xa-cell (xa-hb scr node 2) pw)
        ^I32 cy0 (xa-cell (xa-hb scr node 1) ph)
        ^I32 cy1 (xa-cell (xa-hb scr node 3) ph)
        ^I32 gb (xa-grid-base nn)
        ^:mut ^I32 cy cy0
        ^:mut ^I32 cx 0
        ^:mut ^I32 e 0
        ^:mut ^I32 k 0
        ^:mut ^I32 ov 0
        ^:mut ^I32 best -1
        ^:mut ^I32 bestov 0]
    (while (<= cy cy1)
      (do (set cx cx0)
          (while (<= cx cx1)
            (do (set e (cells-at scr (+ gb (+ (* cy 64) cx))))
                (while (>= e 0)
                  (do (set k (cells-at gp e))
                      (if (or (and (== side 1) (and (< k nt) (!= (xa-hb scr k 9) 0)))
                              (and (== side 0) (and (>= k nt) (!= k node))))
                        (if (== (xa-node-cand scr node k) 1)
                          (do (set ov (ev-overlap-small (xa-hb scr node 0) (xa-hb scr node 1) (xa-hb scr node 2) (xa-hb scr node 3)
                                                        (xa-hb scr k 0) (xa-hb scr k 1) (xa-hb scr k 2) (xa-hb scr k 3)))
                              (if (or (> ov bestov) (and (== ov bestov) (and (>= best 0) (< k best))))
                                (do (set bestov ov)
                                    (set best k))))))
                      (set e (cells-at gp (+ e 1)))))
                (set cx (+ cx 1))))
          (set cy (+ cy 1))))
    (return best)))

(defn ^I32 xa-attach [^:mut ^Cells scr ^I32 nn ^Cells gp ^I32 nt ^I32 no ^I32 pw ^I32 ph ^Cells etext ^:mut ^Cells feats
                      ^:mut ^Cells ta ^:mut ^Cells tb ^:mut ^Cells tt]
  (comment "What no step matched but a word of the other source COVERS: an OCR word that is a candidate of a text-layer word (the")
  (comment "word is longer than the pairing steps reach: `Section2.1` read as three words, a whole line whose spaces the font")
  (comment "does not map) joins that word's group as a split, and a text-layer word that is a candidate of an OCR word joins its")
  (comment "group as a merged one. Without this the covered words would be OCR-only or text-only groups of their own, and")
  (comment "arbitration (P7.3) would write the same text twice (D253).")
  (let [^:mut ^I32 j nt
        ^:mut ^I32 k 0
        ^:mut ^I32 layer 0
        ^:mut ^I32 sim 0
        ^:mut ^I32 cur 0]
    (while (< j (+ nt no))
      (do (if (== (xa-a scr nn 4 j) 0)
            (do (set k (xa-best scr nn gp nt j pw ph 1))
                (if (>= k 0)
                  (do (xa-union scr nn k j)
                      (xa-as scr nn 4 j 1)
                      (set cur (xa-a scr nn 1 k))
                      (xa-as scr nn 1 k (bit-or cur 4))
                      (set cur (xa-a scr nn 1 j))
                      (xa-as scr nn 1 j (bit-or cur 4))
                      (xa-as scr nn 11 0 k)
                      (xa-as scr nn 13 0 j)
                      (set sim (xa-sim scr nn 11 0 1 13 0 1 etext 0 ta tb tt))
                      (set layer 1)
                      (if (== (xa-hb scr k 9) 2) (set layer 2))
                      (if (== layer 1) (xa-put scr j (xo-sim-text) sim feats))
                      (if (== layer 2) (xa-put scr j (xo-sim-hidden) sim feats))))))
          (set j (+ j 1))))
    (set k 0)
    (while (< k nt)
      (do (if (and (!= (xa-hb scr k 9) 0) (== (xa-a scr nn 4 k) 0))
            (do (set j (xa-best scr nn gp nt k pw ph 0))
                (if (>= j 0)
                  (do (xa-union scr nn k j)
                      (xa-as scr nn 4 k 1)
                      (set cur (xa-a scr nn 1 k))
                      (xa-as scr nn 1 k (bit-or cur 8))
                      (set cur (xa-a scr nn 1 j))
                      (xa-as scr nn 1 j (bit-or cur 8))))))
          (set k (+ k 1))))
    (return 0)))

(defn ^I32 xa-cluster [^:mut ^Cells scr ^I32 nn ^Cells gp ^I32 nt ^I32 no ^I32 pw ^I32 ph]
  (comment "Join the OCR words no step matched with the overlapping OCR words of other runs.")
  (let [^I32 gb (xa-grid-base nn)
        ^:mut ^I32 j nt
        ^:mut ^I32 cx 0
        ^:mut ^I32 cy 0
        ^:mut ^I32 cx0 0
        ^:mut ^I32 cx1 0
        ^:mut ^I32 cy1 0
        ^:mut ^I32 e 0
        ^:mut ^I32 k 0]
    (while (< j (+ nt no))
      (do (if (== (xa-a scr nn 4 j) 0)
            (do (set cx0 (xa-cell (xa-hb scr j 0) pw))
                (set cx1 (xa-cell (xa-hb scr j 2) pw))
                (set cy (xa-cell (xa-hb scr j 1) ph))
                (set cy1 (xa-cell (xa-hb scr j 3) ph))
                (while (<= cy cy1)
                  (do (set cx cx0)
                      (while (<= cx cx1)
                        (do (set e (cells-at scr (+ gb (+ (* cy 64) cx))))
                            (while (>= e 0)
                              (do (set k (cells-at gp e))
                                  (if (and (>= k nt) (!= k j))
                                    (if (!= (xa-hb scr k 11) (xa-hb scr j 11))
                                      (if (== (xa-node-cand scr j k) 1)
                                        (xa-union scr nn j k))))
                                  (set e (cells-at gp (+ e 1)))))
                            (set cx (+ cx 1))))
                      (set cy (+ cy 1))))))
          (set j (+ j 1))))
    (return 0)))

;; ------------------------------------------------------------- the lines

(defn ^I32 xa-pos [^Cells scr ^I32 node ^I32 rot ^I32 dir]
  (comment "A node's position along a line whose baseline is at `rot`: the centre projected on the reading axis, negated for a")
  (comment "right-to-left line (so every line is read in logical order).")
  (let [^I64 cx (i64 (+ (xa-hb scr node 0) (xa-hb scr node 2)))
        ^I64 cy (i64 (+ (xa-hb scr node 1) (xa-hb scr node 3)))
        ^I64 v (- (mul64 cx (i64 (ev-cos rot))) (mul64 cy (i64 (ev-sin rot))))
        ^I32 p (i32 (quot v (i64 131072)))]
    (if (== dir 1) (return (- 0 p)))
    (return p)))

(defn ^I32 xa-extent [^:mut ^Cells scr ^I32 nn ^I32 node ^I32 rot ^I32 pos]
  (comment "Set node's extent along a line at `rot` (array 14 its start, 15 its end): its position `pos` less and plus the half of")
  (comment "its box projected on the line's axis.")
  (let [^I64 w (i64 (- (xa-hb scr node 2) (xa-hb scr node 0)))
        ^I64 h (i64 (- (xa-hb scr node 3) (xa-hb scr node 1)))
        ^:mut ^I32 c (ev-cos rot)
        ^:mut ^I32 sn (ev-sin rot)]
    (if (< c 0) (set c (- 0 c)))
    (if (< sn 0) (set sn (- 0 sn)))
    (let [^I32 e (i32 (quot (add64 (mul64 w (i64 c)) (mul64 h (i64 sn))) (i64 131072)))]
      (xa-as scr nn 14 node (- pos e))
      (xa-as scr nn 15 node (+ pos e))
      (return 0))))

(defn ^I32 xa-run-lines [^:mut ^Cells scr ^I32 nn ^I32 nt ^I32 na ^I32 nruns ^Cells etext ^:mut ^Cells feats
                         ^:mut ^Cells dp ^:mut ^Cells ta ^:mut ^Cells tb ^:mut ^Cells tt]
  (comment "Every text-layer line: its OCR words (`ord[0, na)` is the assigned ones sorted by line), then the passes.")
  (let [^:mut ^I32 i 0
        ^:mut ^I32 a 0
        ^:mut ^I32 b 0
        ^:mut ^I32 lid 0
        ^:mut ^I32 lo 0
        ^:mut ^I32 hi 0
        ^:mut ^I32 mid 0
        ^:mut ^I32 bc 0
        ^:mut ^I32 t 0
        ^:mut ^I32 node 0
        ^:mut ^I32 rot 0
        ^:mut ^I32 dir 0
        ^:mut ^I32 layer 0
        ^:mut ^I32 n 0
        ^:mut ^I32 rank 0
        ^:mut ^I32 m 0
        ^:mut ^I32 pos 0
        ^:mut ^I32 ol 0]
    (while (< i nt)
      (do (if (== (xa-hb scr i 9) 0)
            (set i (+ i 1))
            (do (set a i)
                (set lid (xa-hb scr i 10))
                (set b (+ i 1))
                (comment "the run goes on over the words with the same line, skipping the ones that are not candidates")
                (set t (+ i 1))
                (while (and (< t nt) (or (== (xa-hb scr t 9) 0) (== (xa-hb scr t 10) lid)))
                  (do (if (!= (xa-hb scr t 9) 0) (set b (+ t 1)))
                      (set t (+ t 1))))
                (set rot (xa-hb scr a 4))
                (set dir (xa-hb scr a 5))
                (comment "the line's OCR block: ord is sorted by oline, so find its first and its count")
                (set lo 0)
                (set hi na)
                (while (< lo hi)
                  (do (set mid (quot (+ lo hi) 2))
                      (set node (xa-a scr nn 6 mid))
                      (set ol (xa-a scr nn 2 node))
                      (if (< ol lid)
                        (set lo (+ mid 1))
                        (set hi mid))))
                (set bc 0)
                (set ol lid)
                (while (and (< (+ lo bc) na) (== ol lid))
                  (do (set node (xa-a scr nn 6 (+ lo bc)))
                      (set ol (xa-a scr nn 2 node))
                      (if (== ol lid) (set bc (+ bc 1)))))
                (set t 0)
                (while (< t bc)
                  (do (set node (xa-a scr nn 6 (+ lo t)))
                      (xa-as scr nn 12 t node)
                      (set pos (xa-pos scr node rot dir))
                      (xa-as scr nn 5 node pos)
                      (xa-extent scr nn node rot pos)
                      (set t (+ t 1))))
                (set t a)
                (while (< t b)
                  (do (set pos (xa-pos scr t rot dir))
                      (xa-as scr nn 5 t pos)
                      (xa-extent scr nn t rot pos)
                      (set t (+ t 1))))
                (if (> bc 1) (xa-msort scr nn 12 0 bc 5))
                (set layer 1)
                (while (<= layer 2)
                  (do (set n 0)
                      (set t a)
                      (while (< t b)
                        (do (if (== (xa-hb scr t 9) layer)
                              (do (xa-as scr nn 11 n t)
                                  (set n (+ n 1))))
                            (set t (+ t 1))))
                      (if (and (> n 0) (> bc 0))
                        (do (set rank 0)
                            (while (< rank nruns)
                              (do (set m 0)
                                  (set t 0)
                                  (while (< t bc)
                                    (do (set node (xa-a scr nn 12 t))
                                        (if (== (xa-a scr nn 3 node) rank)
                                          (do (xa-as scr nn 13 m node)
                                              (set m (+ m 1))))
                                        (set t (+ t 1))))
                                  (if (> m 0)
                                    (xa-align scr nn n m layer rank etext feats dp ta tb tt))
                                  (set rank (+ rank 1))))))
                      (set layer (+ layer 1))))
                (set i b)))))
    (return 0)))

;; ------------------------------------------------------------- the groups

(defn ^I32 xa-emit [^I32 page ^:mut ^Cells scr ^I32 nn ^I32 nt ^I32 no ^I32 w0 ^I32 o0 ^I32 t0 ^I32 t1
                    ^Cells tlines ^Cells etext ^:mut ^Cells refs ^:mut ^Cells cg
                    ^:mut ^Cells ta ^:mut ^Cells tb ^:mut ^Cells tt]
  (comment "Write the groups in the order of their first candidate; answers how many.")
  (let [^I32 total (+ nt no)
        ^:mut ^I32 i 0
        ^:mut ^I32 s 0
        ^:mut ^I32 g 0
        ^:mut ^I32 r 0
        ^:mut ^I32 c 0
        ^:mut ^I32 e 0
        ^:mut ^I32 node 0
        ^:mut ^I32 tcnt 0
        ^:mut ^I32 hcnt 0
        ^:mut ^I32 ocnt 0
        ^:mut ^I32 x0 0
        ^:mut ^I32 y0 0
        ^:mut ^I32 x1 0
        ^:mut ^I32 y1 0
        ^:mut ^I32 rot 0
        ^:mut ^I32 flags 0
        ^:mut ^I32 minrank 0
        ^:mut ^I32 nm 0
        ^:mut ^I32 row 0
        ^:mut ^I32 bestov 0
        ^:mut ^I32 best 0
        ^:mut ^I32 ov 0
        ^:mut ^I32 kind 0
        ^:mut ^I32 sim -1
        ^:mut ^I32 simfold -1]
    (comment "roots, counts, the exclusive scan and the members bucketed by root (stable, so in candidate order)")
    (set i 0)
    (while (< i nn)
      (do (xa-as scr nn 8 i 0)
          (set i (+ i 1))))
    (set i 0)
    (while (< i total)
      (do (set r (xa-find scr nn i))
          (xa-as scr nn 10 i r)
          (if (!= (xa-hb scr i 9) 0)
            (do (set c (xa-a scr nn 8 r))
                (xa-as scr nn 8 r (+ c 1))))
          (set i (+ i 1))))
    (set s 0)
    (set i 0)
    (while (< i total)
      (do (set c (xa-a scr nn 8 i))
          (xa-as scr nn 8 i s)
          (xa-as scr nn 7 i s)
          (set s (+ s c))
          (set i (+ i 1))))
    (xa-as scr nn 8 total s)
    (set i 0)
    (while (< i total)
      (do (if (!= (xa-hb scr i 9) 0)
            (do (set r (xa-a scr nn 10 i))
                (set c (xa-a scr nn 7 r))
                (xa-as scr nn 9 c i)
                (xa-as scr nn 7 r (+ c 1))))
          (set i (+ i 1))))
    (set r 0)
    (while (< r total)
      (do (if (and (!= (xa-hb scr r 9) 0) (== (xa-a scr nn 10 r) r))
            (do (set s (xa-a scr nn 8 r))
                (set e (xa-a scr nn 8 (+ r 1)))
                (set tcnt 0)
                (set hcnt 0)
                (set ocnt 0)
                (set flags 0)
                (set i s)
                (while (< i e)
                  (do (set node (xa-a scr nn 9 i))
                      (set kind (xa-hb scr node 9))
                      (if (== kind 1) (do (xa-as scr nn 11 tcnt node) (set tcnt (+ tcnt 1))))
                      (if (== kind 2) (do (xa-as scr nn 13 hcnt node) (set hcnt (+ hcnt 1))))
                      (if (== kind 3) (do (xa-as scr nn 12 ocnt node) (set ocnt (+ ocnt 1))))
                      (if (== i s)
                        (do (set x0 (xa-hb scr node 0))
                            (set y0 (xa-hb scr node 1))
                            (set x1 (xa-hb scr node 2))
                            (set y1 (xa-hb scr node 3))
                            (set rot (xa-hb scr node 4)))
                        (do (if (< (xa-hb scr node 0) x0) (set x0 (xa-hb scr node 0)))
                            (if (< (xa-hb scr node 1) y0) (set y0 (xa-hb scr node 1)))
                            (if (> (xa-hb scr node 2) x1) (set x1 (xa-hb scr node 2)))
                            (if (> (xa-hb scr node 3) y1) (set y1 (xa-hb scr node 3)))))
                      (set c (xa-a scr nn 1 node))
                      (set flags (bit-or flags c))
                      (set i (+ i 1))))
                (set c (xa-a scr nn 11 0))
                (set e (xa-a scr nn 13 0))
                (set node (xa-a scr nn 12 0))
                (if (> tcnt 0) (set rot (xa-hb scr c 4)))
                (if (and (== tcnt 0) (> hcnt 0)) (set rot (xa-hb scr e 4)))
                (if (and (== tcnt 0) (and (== hcnt 0) (> ocnt 0))) (set rot (xa-hb scr node 4)))
                (if (and (> (+ tcnt hcnt) 0) (== ocnt 0)) (set flags (bit-or flags (plg-text-only))))
                (if (and (> ocnt 0) (== (+ tcnt hcnt) 0)) (set flags (bit-or flags (plg-ocr-only))))
                (set row (cg-new cg page x0 y0 x1 y1 rot))
                (cg-set cg row (cgf-flags) flags)
                (if (> tcnt 0)
                  (do (cg-set cg row (cgf-tfirst) (rf-count refs))
                      (cg-set cg row (cgf-tcount) tcnt)
                      (set i 0)
                      (while (< i tcnt)
                        (do (set node (xa-a scr nn 11 i))
                            (rf-add refs (ea-words) (+ w0 node))
                            (set i (+ i 1))))))
                (if (> ocnt 0)
                  (do (cg-set cg row (cgf-ofirst) (rf-count refs))
                      (cg-set cg row (cgf-ocount) ocnt)
                      (set i 0)
                      (while (< i ocnt)
                        (do (set node (xa-a scr nn 12 i))
                            (rf-add refs (ea-owords) (+ o0 (- node nt)))
                            (set i (+ i 1))))))
                (if (> hcnt 0)
                  (do (cg-set cg row (cgf-hfirst) (rf-count refs))
                      (cg-set cg row (cgf-hcount) hcnt)
                      (set i 0)
                      (while (< i hcnt)
                        (do (set node (xa-a scr nn 13 i))
                            (rf-add refs (ea-words) (+ w0 node))
                            (set i (+ i 1))))))
                (comment "the similarity: the text layer's words (the hidden ones without them) against the lowest run's")
                (set sim -1)
                (set simfold -1)
                (if (and (> ocnt 0) (> (+ tcnt hcnt) 0))
                  (do (set node (xa-a scr nn 12 0))
                      (set minrank (xa-a scr nn 3 node))
                      (set i 0)
                      (while (< i ocnt)
                        (do (set node (xa-a scr nn 12 i))
                            (set c (xa-a scr nn 3 node))
                            (if (< c minrank) (set minrank c))
                            (set i (+ i 1))))
                      (set nm 0)
                      (set i 0)
                      (while (< i ocnt)
                        (do (set node (xa-a scr nn 12 i))
                            (if (== (xa-a scr nn 3 node) minrank)
                              (do (xa-as scr nn 5 nm node)
                                  (set nm (+ nm 1))))
                            (set i (+ i 1))))
                      (if (> tcnt 0)
                        (do (set sim (xa-sim scr nn 11 0 tcnt 5 0 nm etext 0 ta tb tt))
                            (set simfold (xa-sim scr nn 11 0 tcnt 5 0 nm etext 1 ta tb tt)))
                        (do (set sim (xa-sim scr nn 13 0 hcnt 5 0 nm etext 0 ta tb tt))
                            (set simfold (xa-sim scr nn 13 0 hcnt 5 0 nm etext 1 ta tb tt))))))
                (cg-set cg row (cgf-sim) sim)
                (cg-set cg row (cgf-simfold) simfold)
                (comment "the tracer line the group's box overlaps most")
                (set best -1)
                (set bestov 0)
                (set i t0)
                (while (< i t1)
                  (do (if (== (xa-cand x0 y0 x1 y1 rot
                                       (cells-at tlines (+ (* i 20) 1)) (cells-at tlines (+ (* i 20) 2))
                                       (cells-at tlines (+ (* i 20) 3)) (cells-at tlines (+ (* i 20) 4))
                                       (cells-at tlines (+ (* i 20) 9))) 1)
                        (do (set ov (ev-overlap-small x0 y0 x1 y1
                                                      (cells-at tlines (+ (* i 20) 1)) (cells-at tlines (+ (* i 20) 2))
                                                      (cells-at tlines (+ (* i 20) 3)) (cells-at tlines (+ (* i 20) 4))))
                            (if (> ov bestov)
                              (do (set bestov ov)
                                  (set best i)))))
                      (set i (+ i 1))))
                (cg-set cg row (cgf-tline) best)
                (set g (+ g 1))))
          (set r (+ r 1))))
    (return g)))

;; ------------------------------------------------------------- the page

(defn ^I32 xa-lower [^Cells c ^I32 stride ^I32 page]
  (comment "The first row of an arena whose page is at least `page`, the rows being in page order.")
  (let [^:mut ^I32 lo 0
        ^:mut ^I32 hi (quot (cells-len c) stride)
        ^:mut ^I32 mid 0]
    (while (< lo hi)
      (do (set mid (quot (+ lo hi) 2))
          (if (< (cells-at c (* mid stride)) page)
            (set lo (+ mid 1))
            (set hi mid))))
    (return lo)))

(defn ^I32 xa-load-head [^:mut ^Cells scr ^I32 i ^Cells src ^I32 stride ^I32 r]
  (comment "Copy the head of row r of an arena of the given stride (a word's or an OCR word's) into node i.")
  (xa-hbs scr i 0 (cells-at src (+ (* r stride) (hd-x0))))
  (xa-hbs scr i 1 (cells-at src (+ (* r stride) (hd-y0))))
  (xa-hbs scr i 2 (cells-at src (+ (* r stride) (hd-x1))))
  (xa-hbs scr i 3 (cells-at src (+ (* r stride) (hd-y1))))
  (xa-hbs scr i 4 (cells-at src (+ (* r stride) (hd-rot))))
  (xa-hbs scr i 5 (cells-at src (+ (* r stride) (hd-dir))))
  (xa-hbs scr i 6 (cells-at src (+ (* r stride) (hd-tstart))))
  (xa-hbs scr i 7 (cells-at src (+ (* r stride) (hd-tlen))))
  (xa-hbs scr i 8 (cells-at src (+ (* r stride) (hd-feat))))
  (return 0))

(defn ^:pub ^I32 xa-page [^I32 page ^Cells epages ^Cells words ^Cells owords ^Cells tlines ^:mut ^Cells feats ^Cells etext
                          ^:mut ^Cells refs ^:mut ^Cells cg ^:mut ^Cells scr ^:mut ^Cells gp ^:mut ^Cells dp
                          ^:mut ^Cells ta ^:mut ^Cells tb ^:mut ^Cells tt]
  (comment "Align one page. See the head of the file. Answers the number of groups appended to `cg`.")
  (let [^I32 w0 (xa-lower words 24 page)
        ^I32 w1 (xa-lower words 24 (+ page 1))
        ^I32 o0 (xa-lower owords 28 page)
        ^I32 o1 (xa-lower owords 28 (+ page 1))
        ^I32 t0 (xa-lower tlines 20 page)
        ^I32 t1 (xa-lower tlines 20 (+ page 1))
        ^I32 nt (- w1 w0)
        ^I32 no (- o1 o0)
        ^I32 total (+ nt no)
        ^I32 nn (+ total 1)
        ^I32 erow (ev-page-row epages page)
        ^:mut ^I32 pw 1
        ^:mut ^I32 ph 1
        ^:mut ^I32 i 0
        ^:mut ^I32 r 0
        ^:mut ^I32 f 0
        ^:mut ^I32 v 0
        ^:mut ^I32 prun -2
        ^:mut ^I32 rk -1
        ^:mut ^I32 csrc 0
        ^:mut ^I32 na 0]
    (if (== total 0) (return 0))
    (cells-drop scr 0)
    (while (< i (+ (* 28 nn) 4096))
      (do (cells-push scr 0)
          (set i (+ i 1))))
    (cells-drop gp 0)
    (comment "the text layer's heads, kinds and lines")
    (set i 0)
    (while (< i nt)
      (do (set r (+ w0 i))
          (xa-load-head scr i words 24 r)
          (set f (xa-hb scr i 8))
          (set v 0)
          (if (>= f 0)
            (do (set v (fe-get feats f (xt-vis)))
                (if (< v 0) (set v 0))))
          (set csrc (cells-at words (+ (* r 24) (wf-src))))
          (xa-hbs scr i 9 0)
          (if (!= (bit-and csrc (sr-hidden-text)) 0)
            (xa-hbs scr i 9 2)
            (if (== v 0) (xa-hbs scr i 9 1)))
          (set f (cells-at words (+ (* r 24) (hd-line))))
          (if (< f 0) (set f (+ 1000000000 i)))
          (xa-hbs scr i 10 f)
          (set i (+ i 1))))
    (comment "the OCR words' heads and their runs, ranked in order of appearance")
    (set i 0)
    (while (< i no)
      (do (set r (+ o0 i))
          (xa-load-head scr (+ nt i) owords 28 r)
          (xa-hbs scr (+ nt i) 9 3)
          (set f (cells-at owords (+ (* r 28) (owf-run))))
          (xa-hbs scr (+ nt i) 11 f)
          (if (!= f prun)
            (do (set rk (+ rk 1))
                (set prun f)))
          (xa-as scr nn 3 (+ nt i) rk)
          (set i (+ i 1))))
    (comment "the page box (the grid's scale), the union-find and the grid")
    (set i 0)
    (while (< i total)
      (do (if (!= (xa-hb scr i 9) 0)
            (do (if (> (xa-hb scr i 2) pw) (set pw (xa-hb scr i 2)))
                (if (> (xa-hb scr i 3) ph) (set ph (xa-hb scr i 3)))))
          (xa-as scr nn 0 i i)
          (xa-as scr nn 2 i -1)
          (set i (+ i 1))))
    (if (>= erow 0)
      (do (set v (ep-get epages erow (epf-width)))
          (if (> v 0) (set pw v))
          (set v (ep-get epages erow (epf-height)))
          (if (> v 0) (set ph v))))
    (set i 0)
    (while (< i 4096)
      (do (cells-set scr (+ (xa-grid-base nn) i) -1)
          (set i (+ i 1))))
    (set i 0)
    (while (< i total)
      (do (if (!= (xa-hb scr i 9) 0) (xa-grid-add scr nn gp i pw ph))
          (set i (+ i 1))))
    (comment "every OCR word's line, and the OCR words that have one sorted by it (stably: by their order)")
    (set i 0)
    (while (< i no)
      (do (set v (xa-best scr nn gp nt (+ nt i) pw ph 1))
          (if (>= v 0) (set v (xa-hb scr v 10)))
          (xa-as scr nn 2 (+ nt i) v)
          (if (>= v 0)
            (do (xa-as scr nn 6 na (+ nt i))
                (set na (+ na 1))))
          (set i (+ i 1))))
    (if (> na 1) (xa-msort scr nn 6 0 na 2))
    (xa-run-lines scr nn nt na (+ rk 1) etext feats dp ta tb tt)
    (xa-attach scr nn gp nt no pw ph etext feats ta tb tt)
    (xa-cluster scr nn gp nt no pw ph)
    (return (xa-emit page scr nn nt no w0 o0 t0 t1 tlines etext refs cg ta tb tt))))
